\section*{{\cjkfont 繁\hspace{0pt}體\hspace{0pt}中\hspace{0pt}文\hspace{0pt}摘\hspace{0pt}要\hspace{0pt}}}
{\cjkfont\raggedright
本\hspace{0pt}研\hspace{0pt}究\hspace{0pt}探\hspace{0pt}討\hspace{0pt}：\hspace{0pt}在\hspace{0pt}兩\hspace{0pt}個\hspace{0pt}來\hspace{0pt}源\hspace{0pt}鎖\hspace{0pt}定\hspace{0pt}的\hspace{0pt}緊\hspace{0pt}緻\hspace{0pt}虧\hspace{0pt}格\hspace{0pt}二\hspace{0pt}雙\hspace{0pt}曲\hspace{0pt}曲\hspace{0pt}面\hspace{0pt}上\hspace{0pt}，\hspace{0pt}何\hspace{0pt}種\hspace{0pt}精\hspace{0pt}確\hspace{0pt}憑\hspace{0pt}證\hspace{0pt}架\hspace{0pt}構\hspace{0pt}可\hspace{0pt}支\hspace{0pt}援\hspace{0pt}原\hspace{0pt}始\hspace{0pt}閉\hspace{0pt}測\hspace{0pt}地\hspace{0pt}線\hspace{0pt}的\hspace{0pt}所\hspace{0pt}有\hspace{0pt}權\hspace{0pt}判\hspace{0pt}定\hspace{0pt}。\hspace{0pt}研\hspace{0pt}究\hspace{0pt}對\hspace{0pt}象\hspace{0pt}固\hspace{0pt}定\hspace{0pt}為\hspace{0pt} Bolza 目\hspace{0pt}標\hspace{0pt}曲\hspace{0pt}面\hspace{0pt}與\hspace{0pt}一\hspace{0pt}個\hspace{0pt}非\hspace{0pt}算\hspace{0pt}術\hspace{0pt}控\hspace{0pt}制\hspace{0pt}曲\hspace{0pt}面\hspace{0pt}，\hspace{0pt}動\hspace{0pt}力\hspace{0pt}學\hspace{0pt}子\hspace{0pt}型\hspace{0pt}固\hspace{0pt}定\hspace{0pt}為\hspace{0pt}單\hspace{0pt}位\hspace{0pt}速\hspace{0pt}率\hspace{0pt}的\hspace{0pt}物\hspace{0pt}理\hspace{0pt}基\hspace{0pt}底\hspace{0pt}測\hspace{0pt}地\hspace{0pt}時\hspace{0pt}間\hspace{0pt}、磁\hspace{0pt}場\hspace{0pt}參\hspace{0pt}數\hspace{0pt} $b=1/2$ 及\hspace{0pt}有\hspace{0pt}號\hspace{0pt}磁\hspace{0pt}場\hspace{0pt}的\hspace{0pt}偶\hspace{0pt}數\hspace{0pt}子\hspace{0pt}序\hspace{0pt}列\hspace{0pt}；\hspace{0pt}共\hspace{0pt}同\hspace{0pt}截\hspace{0pt}斷\hspace{0pt}值\hspace{0pt}維\hspace{0pt}持\hspace{0pt}為\hspace{0pt} $\Lambda=21/10$，\hspace{0pt}且\hspace{0pt}不\hspace{0pt}得\hspace{0pt}依\hspace{0pt}已\hspace{0pt}知\hspace{0pt}方\hspace{0pt}向\hspace{0pt}重\hspace{0pt}新\hspace{0pt}調\hspace{0pt}整\hspace{0pt}。\hspace{0pt}本\hspace{0pt}研\hspace{0pt}究\hspace{0pt}實\hspace{0pt}際\

The two project objects originate in a substantial but heterogeneous literature. Nazarenko (2013)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S01 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S01}
 supplies the compact genus-two octagon-family and generator context from which the frozen control is drawn. Aigon-Dupuy et al.~(2005)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S02 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S02}
 provide peer-reviewed family-level context for genus-two hyperbolic octagons and Fuchsian descriptions. For the target, Aurich et al.~(1991)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S05 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S05}
 provide regular-octagon matrices, a length relation, and a periodic-orbit enumeration precedent, while Katz et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S08 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S08}
 provide arithmetic-Fuchsian and quaternion-order context for the Bolza surface. Grácio and Sousa Ramos (2010)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S09 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S09}
 connect symbolic dynamics and fundamental-group words to genus-two length-spectrum computation. These contributions support objects and candidate-generation contexts; they are not treated as completed P33 owner censuses.

The target is similarly treated through bounded complementary context. Aurich et al.~(1991)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S05 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S05}
 provide regular-octagon periodic-orbit and matrix context, and Katz et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S08 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S08}
 provide exact arithmetic and quaternion-order context for Bolza. Jenni (1984)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S06 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S06}
 remains PLAUSIBLE, page-unpinned, and context-only in the frozen verifier; it is not used here to assert an exact systole theorem or formula. Schmutz (1993)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S07 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S07}
 supplies broader extremal and systolic context without independently validating the project replay inequality. Thus object identity, arithmetic characterization, systolic context, and below-cutoff owner closure remain separate evidence surfaces.

Strohmaier and Uski (2013, corrected 2018)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S16 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S16}
 illustrate a separation among bounded computation, error control, and completeness reasoning for spectral objects on hyperbolic surfaces; their correction remains visible and their determinant endpoint is outside P33. Johansson (2017)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S17 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S17}
 presents arbitrary-precision midpoint-radius arithmetic with explicit error radii. Rump (2010)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S18 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S18}
 surveys rigorous verification using floating-point computation. These works support proof-bearing enclosure discipline for appropriate numerical predicates, but interval arithmetic does not decide group conjugacy or primitivity.

Correction and locator boundaries were carried forward exactly. The Takeuchi record retains its correction binding (Takeuchi, 1975)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S03 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S03}
, and the Strohmaier-Uski record retains its 2018 correction binding (Strohmaier and Uski, 2013, corrected 2018)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S16 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S16}
. Epstein and Holt (2006)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S12 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S12}
 retains pages 287--305. Jenni (1984)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S06 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S06}
 remains PLAUSIBLE, page-unpinned, and context-only.

The literature supports the three-package architecture only at component and precedent level. Voight (2009)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S10 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S10}
 and Despré et al.~(2023)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S11 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S11}
 support different domain or presentation pathways. Epstein and Holt (2006)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S12 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S12}
 and Lysenok (1990)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S13 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S13}
 support conjugacy and root-decision components. Cherubini et al.~(2022)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S14 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S14}
 and Erlandsson and Souto (2024)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S15 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S15}
 motivate separate primitive, repetition, reciprocal, and inverse-pair semantics. Strohmaier and Uski (2013, corrected 2018)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S16 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S16}
, Johansson (2017)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S17 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S17}
, and Rump (2010)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S18 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S18}
 support rigorous predicate and enclosure discipline. Hoffman et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S19 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S19}
 and Hales et al.~(2017)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S20 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S20}
 support the broader producer-validator pattern. None supplies the missing P33 implementation or scientific result.

The frozen literature supports genus-two octagon objects, Bolza context, and candidate-generation precedents, but it does not itself identify unique primitive inverse-paired owners. Nazarenko (2013)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S01 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S01}
 and Aigon-Dupuy et al.~(2005)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S02 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S02}
 bound the control-family context. Aurich et al.~(1991)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S05 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S05}
, Katz et al.~(2016)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S08 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S08}
, and Grácio and Sousa Ramos (2010)
% ARS-CITE source_ids=P33-S09 anchor=none claim_to_passage=INCONCLUSIVE
\citep{P33-S09}
 bound complementary target and candidate-generation contexts. No cited source is converted into a project-level full-conjugacy, maximal-root, inverse-pair, or completeness certificate.

\begin{enumerate}
\def\labelenumi{\arabic{enumi}.}
\tightlist
\item
  \textbf{Execution status:} not run, rejected at freeze, bounded-incomplete, not evaluable, or completed under a frozen contract.
\item
  \textbf{Scientific content:} per-surface owner and completeness outcomes, only if actually certified.
\item
  \textbf{Roadmap interpretation:} Route-A or Route-B assessment, only under a separately authorized roadmap gate.
\end{enumerate}
